{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CUTOVER HELD — operator decision, recorded before acting.\n\nS8 does NOT proceed until Bedrock is CONFIRMED to clear the S6 parity bar (ticket 0d76).\n\nCutover is AUTHORIZED IN PRINCIPLE once there are no known bugs in the Bedrock implementation, and\nthat narrow condition is ALREADY SATISFIED: every open bug in this epic sits in the parity HARNESS\n(62ac, 635f) or in provider-agnostic caching (f81d, e3cd). None is in the Bedrock provider code, and\nthe Bedrock implementation bugs 03b0 and 7b22 are closed. What holds S8 is therefore the bar\nconfirmation, not a Bedrock defect.\n\nWHERE THE BAR STANDS. The live paired run measured Bedrock as FAILING both slots, but one of the three\nfailures is a confirmed harness defect and the other two do not show Bedrock is worse:\n  * frontier false-accept \"FAIL\" 0.786 -> 0.929 is the INVERTED metric (62ac). The quantity computed is\n    specificity — safe items correctly NOT blocked, higher-is-better — while the report fails the run\n    when it RISES. Bedrock false-fired LESS and was penalised for the improvement.\n  * the three genuine decision flips ALL FAVOUR BEDROCK: standard caught a gold-BLOCK Anthropic missed;\n    frontier declined to fire on two gold-ADVISORY cases Anthropic false-fired on.\n  * frontier verdict agreement 0.929 against the 0.95 floor is the one failure not yet explained.\n\nNEXT, and deliberately cheap: 62ac and 635f are being fixed now, after which the ALREADY-RECORDED live\nrun is re-scored OFFLINE with corrected metrics — zero model calls, zero spend. The recorded results are\nat src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json, 30 per-case records per slot.\n\nAn Anthropic-vs-Anthropic noise-floor run was proposed and NOT APPROVED: further expensive evals require\njustification beyond caution or establishing a floor. The honest consequence, stated rather than buried:\nwe cannot currently say whether zero decision flips is achievable by ANY provider pair, including\nAnthropic against itself. If flips still fail after the re-score, that is a question about the BAR, not\nabout Bedrock, and the answer is to revisit the criterion — not to buy another run.\n\nDO NOT claim this ticket until 0d76 records a cleared bar."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785720650200607001,"uuid":"bf5b09fd-5361-4a95-a675-2a3ffad0bc8d"}